3a.3 Average US Electricity Emissions
To establish a national baseline, we calculated the average emissions across the United States. By weighting each state’s emissions (pounds of CO₂ per MWh) by its total electricity generation, we determined that the US power grid emits an average of 785 pounds of CO₂ per MWh of electricity produced.


Show All Code
# 3a.4: "rarest" = primary source for the fewest states. Slicing the three
# smallest counts keeps any ties at the cutoff (here none: the third-rarest
# count is 4 and the next source has 5 states).
rarest_sources &lt;- EIA_SEP_REPORT |&gt;
  count(primary_source, name = "n_states") |&gt;
  slice_min(n_states, n = 3)

rare_source_tbl &lt;- EIA_SEP_REPORT |&gt;
  inner_join(rarest_sources, join_by(primary_source)) |&gt;
  group_by(primary_source) |&gt;
  mutate(
    # generation-weighted, so a big producer counts more than a small one
    avg_price = weighted.mean(electricity_price_MWh, generation_MWh),
    group_label = paste0(
      primary_source, ": ", n_states, if_else(n_states == 1, " state", " states"),
      ", average ", dollar(avg_price, accuracy = 1), " / MWh"
    )
  ) |&gt;
  ungroup() |&gt;
  arrange(n_states, primary_source, desc(electricity_price_MWh))

rare_source_prices &lt;- rare_source_tbl |&gt;
  distinct(primary_source, n_states, avg_price)

